&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 202, 250);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(115, 115, 229);&quot;&gt;Are you an operations research engineer ready to take on some of the most complex supply chain and commercial challenges in the country?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Bash, we build the mathematical models that decide how thousands of orders move through the logistics network and what we do next for every customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this pivotal role, you will lead the design and implementation of advanced models that optimise our rapidly scaling company. You&#39;ll be at the forefront of developing algorithms and machine learning models that support everything across domains at Bash, while conducting sensitivity analyses and scenario planning to ensure our systems respond dynamically to changing inputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not just fulfilling orders; we&#39;re building our own courier network, optimising allocation across 3,500 stores,continuously refining algorithms to deliver the lowest prices with the fastest turnaround times, and building a decision engine that chooses the next best action for every customer and every unit of stock. This is a playground for an engineer who thrives on solving complex, real-world problems and wants to make a tangible impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 202, 250);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(115, 115, 229);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(70, 70, 232);&quot;&gt;WHAT WE OWN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fulfillment Centre Allocation Algorithms&lt;/strong&gt;: Own and develop these essential tools to optimise our network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Predict parcel counts, driver requirements, and store units with precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommendation Engine: &lt;/strong&gt;Recommend the right product to the right customer at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simulation Environment:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Build out a simulation environment to test network design and algorithm changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General Analytical Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide deep analytical insights to support ongoing and future initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 202, 250);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(115, 115, 229);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(70, 70, 232);&quot;&gt;OPERATIONS RESEARCH ENGINEER EXPERIENCE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years’ in a similar role, ideally in a retail environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Operations Research, Industrial Engineering, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or a related field. Ph.D. preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in statistical analysis and programming (Python, R, SQL), with a preference for machine learning expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of supply chain analytics, including areas like inventory management, transportation, and network optimization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to pricing, markdown, or elasticity modelling is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in multi-objective optimisation and linear programming, adept at data visualisation (using tools like Seaborn or ggplot) and the ability to explain a model to someone who will not read the mathematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of end-to-end supply chain processes, including demand forecasting, inventory management, operations, logistics, and network design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A general understanding of what it entails to take a model into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is perfect for an operations research engineer who loves to build, tweak, and apply their expertise to complex mathematical problems. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
